// prism_ui_stat -- dashboard stat/metric CARDS (prism/ui/, milestone MB.13): a single stat with a
// prefix/suffix, a stat with a trend indicator, a current-vs-previous comparison, a titled card
// wrapper, and a responsive grid of cards. Every one is a COMPOSITION over the closed 22-primitive
// vocabulary (widget/), built through prism_ui_kit.nova's helpers wherever they fit -- no new
// PrismNodeKind (PRISM_SPEC.md axiom A7), the same discipline every prism_ui_*.nova file follows.
// This is the Ant Design `Statistic` + `Card` + `Row`/`Col` grid family: the tiles seen on every
// admin dashboard's top row.
//
// ── THIS IS NOT prism_ui_data.prism_ui_stat, AND THE OVERLAP IS DELIBERATE, NOT MISSED ──────────
// Grepped before writing a line of this file (CLAUDE.md's "does this already exist" discipline):
// `prism_ui_data.nova` (MB.3) already has a `PrismStatTrend` (StatUp/StatDown/StatFlat) and a
// `prism_ui_stat(label, value, delta: string?, trend)` that folds label+value+delta+trend into
// ONE shape. This file is a DIFFERENT, richer FAMILY, not a duplicate of that one function:
//   - `prism_st_stat` here separates "prefix/suffix around the value" (currency symbols, units --
//     Ant's own `Statistic` `prefix`/`suffix` props, e.g. "$" / "USD") from "trend" entirely --
//     MB.3's single function conflates a trend delta with the value's own formatting, so a stat
//     needing "$" prefix and no trend at all (a running total, a count) has no honest fit there.
//   - `prism_st_trend` and `prism_st_comparison` are two-more DISTINCT rendered shapes ("value +
//     icon + change text" vs "current vs previous, side by side") that MB.3's one function cannot
//     express as different layouts -- both there always render as `stack[label, value, delta?]`.
//   - `prism_st_card` / `prism_st_dashboard` (titled wrapper + responsive grid) have NO equivalent
//     in `prism_ui_data.nova` at all -- that file has no notion of grouping stats into a card or a
//     dashboard row.
// The precedent for two components sharing a domain across two files without collision is already
// tested in this codebase: `prism_ui_timeline.nova`'s own header records the identical situation
// (its `PrismTlStatus` vs `prism_ui_data`'s `PrismTimelineStatus`, 3 of 4 variant names shared) and
// the direct probe proving two closed enums sharing bare variant names in different files do not
// collide in NOVA's flat LLVM symbol space (constructors are mangled per-enum). This file's own
// type name (`PrismStDirection`, not `PrismStatTrend`) and function prefix (`prism_st_*`, not
// `prism_ui_stat`/`prism_stat_trend_*`) keep both components callable side by side with zero
// ambiguity at any call site, following that exact precedent rather than re-deriving it.
//
// Likewise, `prism_st_card` is NOT a duplicate of `prism_ui_media.prism_ui_card` (MB.4): that card
// is a general media surface (`title + optional body text + optional media node + optional action
// buttons`, in that fixed order, collapsing to the title alone when nothing else is supplied). A
// stat card's actual shape is different on purpose -- a title header over an ARBITRARY, CALLER-
// SUPPLIED list of already-built stat nodes (one or many `prism_st_stat`/`prism_st_trend`/
// `prism_st_comparison` results, or any other `PrismNode` -- validated generically, see below), not
// a single body/media/actions triple. Reusing `prism_ui_card` here would force a stat-bearing
// caller to smuggle every stat into that function's single `body: string?` slot, discarding
// structure the caller already built.
//
// ── WHY PrismStDirection's ICONS REUSE prism_ui_data's EXACT MAPPING, NOT COINCIDENCE ────────────
// `StUp -> chevron_up`, `StDown -> chevron_down`, `StFlat -> minus` is the identical assignment
// `prism_stat_trend_icon` (prism_ui_data.nova) already made for the identical semantic idea
// ("value went up / down / did not move"). Re-deriving a DIFFERENT mapping here for the same
// concept would be arbitrary and would make the two dashboards' trend icons disagree for no
// reason; reusing the established, already-KAT-proven mapping is a deliberate consistency choice,
// not an oversight that the two enums happen to look alike.
//
// ── WHY prefix/suffix ARE PLAIN STRINGS, NOT PrismIcon ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Ant Design's `Statistic` `prefix`/`suffix` props are most commonly a currency symbol, a unit
// ("$", "%", "USD", "/mo") or occasionally an icon -- but the closed 12-icon set (prism_content.nova)
// has no currency glyphs at all, and forcing every prefix/suffix through `PrismIcon` would make the
// overwhelmingly common case (a unit string) unrepresentable while adding nothing for the rare
// icon case (a caller wanting an icon there can still compose one via `prism_st_card`'s child list
// or a `prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_icon_text` row placed alongside). `string?` is the honest, minimal
// typing for what this prop actually carries here.
//
// ── WHY A PRESENT-BUT-BLANK prefix/suffix DEGRADES TO ABSENT, NOT A RENDERED EMPTY LABEL ─────────
// Same tolerance as `prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_field_row`'s `note: string?` and `prism_fb_alert`'s
// `detail: string?`: "no prefix" and "prefix is the empty string" are different facts, and treating
// `Some("")` as "render a blank label in the value row" would be indistinguishable from a rendering
// bug to anyone reading the output. `_prism_st_opt_part` is the ONE place this degradation happens,
// shared by both `st_prefix` and `st_suffix` rather than re-derived per call site.
//
// ── WHY prism_st_card/prism_st_dashboard VALIDATE "ANY PrismNode", NOT "MUST BE A prism_st_* NODE" ─
// There is no runtime way to distinguish "a PrismNode built by `prism_st_stat`" from "a PrismNode
// built by anything else" -- every constructor in this codebase funnels through the same
// `prism_node_new`, and the resulting struct carries no provenance tag. Requiring "must be a stat
// node" is therefore not enforceable, and even if it were, a caller legitimately wanting a plain
// label or a divider between cards would be blocked for no real safety gain. Both functions instead
// take the same generic, already-proven-safe guard `prism_tk_tag_group`/`prism_tl_timeline` use:
// `type_name(x) != "PrismNode"` per element, naming the offending index and actual type. The KAT
// proves this with a deliberately MIXED list (real stat cards plus one plain label), mirroring
// `prism_ui_token`'s own tag-group test for the identical "accepts any PrismNode" contract.
//
// ── WHY prism_st_card's GAP IS A FIXED `prism_gap(some(8))`, NOT A FLEXIBLE prism_gap(none()) ────
// A flexible gap (`gap()`, "absorbs remaining space") is for pushing content apart inside a
// container with free space to distribute -- the wrong tool for a small, constant visual breathing
// space between a card's title and its body, which is what every real card design (Ant's own
// `Card`, this codebase's `prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_spacer`) uses a fixed gap for. 8 is a modest,
// unremarkable spacing value with no other significance; it is named (`PRISM_ST_CARD_GAP`) rather
// than left as a bare literal so a future design-token pass has one place to change it.
//
// PUBLIC API
//   Direction (closed, 3 values -- reuses prism_ui_data's icon mapping, see header)
//     PrismStDirection                                    StUp() | StDown() | StFlat()
//     prism_st_up() / prism_st_down() / prism_st_flat()   cross-module ctors
//     prism_st_direction_name(d) -> string     exhaustive: "up" | "down" | "flat"
//     prism_st_direction_icon(d) -> PrismIcon  exhaustive, no wildcard, all 3 pairwise distinct
//   Components (all Result<PrismNode>; every one validates, none fails silently)
//     prism_st_stat(st_label, st_value, st_prefix: string?, st_suffix: string?)
//       -> stack[band[prefix?, value, suffix?], label]; rejects an empty st_label/st_value; a
//       present-but-empty st_prefix/st_suffix degrades to absent (see header).
//     prism_st_trend(st_label, st_value, st_direction, st_change)
//       -> stack[band[value, icon, change], label]; rejects an empty st_label/st_value/st_change.
//     prism_st_comparison(st_label, st_current, st_previous)
//       -> stack[band[current, "vs", previous], label]; rejects an empty st_label/st_current/
//       st_previous.
//     prism_st_card(title, children: list)
//       -> stack[title_label, gap(8), ...children]; `children` is a bare list (runtime-checked,
//       see header), rejects an empty title, an empty children list, and a non-PrismNode element
//       (named by index and actual type).
//     prism_st_dashboard(cards: list)
//       -> flow(cards); `cards` is a bare list (same runtime-checked discipline), rejects an empty
//       list and a non-PrismNode element (named by index and actual type).

import prism_arrange
import prism_content
import prism_ui_kit

// ── Direction: closed, 3 values (see header) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
enum PrismStDirection
    StUp()
    StDown()
    StFlat()

fn prism_st_up() -> PrismStDirection
    StUp()
fn prism_st_down() -> PrismStDirection
    StDown()
fn prism_st_flat() -> PrismStDirection
    StFlat()

// Exhaustive, no wildcard arm -- adding a 4th direction without a case here is a compile error.
fn prism_st_direction_name(d: PrismStDirection) -> string
    match d
        StUp() => "up"
        StDown() => "down"
        StFlat() => "flat"

// Exhaustive, no wildcard arm. Reuses prism_ui_data's exact StatUp/StatDown/StatFlat -> icon
// mapping (see header) -- the KAT proves all 3 stay pairwise distinct.
fn prism_st_direction_icon(d: PrismStDirection) -> PrismIcon
    match d
        StUp() => prism_content.prism_icon_chevron_up()
        StDown() => prism_content.prism_icon_chevron_down()
        StFlat() => prism_content.prism_icon_minus()

// ── Shared: an optional text part that degrades a blank Some("") to absent (see header) ─────────
fn _prism_st_opt_part(text: string?) -> Result<list>
    match text
        None => ok([])
        Some(t) =>
            if len(t) == 0
                return ok([])
            let node = prism_content.prism_label(t)?
            ok([node])

// ── Single stat: optional prefix/suffix around the value, label below ───────────────────────────
fn prism_st_stat(st_label: string, st_value: string, st_prefix: string?, st_suffix: string?) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(st_label) == 0
        return err("prism_st_stat: st_label must not be empty")
    if len(st_value) == 0
        return err("prism_st_stat: st_value must not be empty")
    let label_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_label)?
    let value_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_value)?
    let prefix_parts = _prism_st_opt_part(st_prefix)?
    let suffix_parts = _prism_st_opt_part(st_suffix)?
    let value_row = prism_arrange.prism_band([...prefix_parts, value_node, ...suffix_parts])?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([value_row, label_node])

// ── Stat with a trend indicator: value + direction icon + change text, label below ──────────────
fn prism_st_trend(st_label: string, st_value: string, st_direction: PrismStDirection, st_change: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(st_label) == 0
        return err("prism_st_trend: st_label must not be empty")
    if len(st_value) == 0
        return err("prism_st_trend: st_value must not be empty")
    if len(st_change) == 0
        return err("prism_st_trend: st_change must not be empty")
    let label_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_label)?
    let value_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_value)?
    let icon_node = prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_st_direction_icon(st_direction))?
    let change_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_change)?
    let value_row = prism_arrange.prism_band([value_node, icon_node, change_node])?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([value_row, label_node])

// ── Side-by-side comparison: current vs previous, label below ───────────────────────────────────
// The literal "vs" separator is a plain label, not a caller-supplied string -- this component's
// entire identity is "these two values are being compared", so the separator is fixed rather than
// a 4th parameter for a word that is always the same.
fn prism_st_comparison(st_label: string, st_current: string, st_previous: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(st_label) == 0
        return err("prism_st_comparison: st_label must not be empty")
    if len(st_current) == 0
        return err("prism_st_comparison: st_current must not be empty")
    if len(st_previous) == 0
        return err("prism_st_comparison: st_previous must not be empty")
    let label_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_label)?
    let current_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_current)?
    let vs_node = prism_content.prism_label("vs")?
    let previous_node = prism_content.prism_label(st_previous)?
    let compare_row = prism_arrange.prism_band([current_node, vs_node, previous_node])?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([compare_row, label_node])

// A small, constant title-to-body breathing space -- see header for why this is fixed, not flexible.
let PRISM_ST_CARD_GAP = 8

// ── Card: a titled wrapper around any caller-built stat content ──────────────────────────────────
// `children` is a bare `list` (not `list<PrismNode>` -- mirroring prism_node.nova's own
// self-referential-generic caution, and prism_tk_tag_group's/prism_tl_timeline's identical choice
// for the identical reason), so every element is guarded with the same `type_name(...) !=
// "PrismNode"` check, naming the offending index and actual type on rejection. See header for why
// this accepts ANY PrismNode rather than requiring a `prism_st_*` provenance that cannot be checked.
fn prism_st_card(title: string, children: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(title) == 0
        return err("prism_st_card: title must not be empty")
    if len(children) == 0
        return err("prism_st_card: children must not be empty")
    for idx, c in children
        if type_name(c) != "PrismNode"
            return err("prism_st_card: child " + str(idx) + " is not a PrismNode (got " + type_name(c) + ")")
    let title_node = prism_content.prism_label(title)?
    let gap_node = prism_arrange.prism_gap(some(PRISM_ST_CARD_GAP))?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([title_node, gap_node, ...children])

// ── Dashboard: a responsive grid (flow) of stat cards ────────────────────────────────────────────
// `flow` (not `stack`/`band`) because PRISM_SPEC.md §7 defines it as "inline children that wrap" --
// the exact responsive-row-that-wraps behaviour a dashboard's top row of cards needs at narrow
// widths, and the layout §11 has no media-query cascade to rescue a fixed `band` at (same
// reasoning `prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_labeled`'s header already applies to why it stacks rather than
// bands). Same generic "any PrismNode" validation as `prism_st_card`, for the identical reason.
fn prism_st_dashboard(cards: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(cards) == 0
        return err("prism_st_dashboard: cards must not be empty")
    for idx, c in cards
        if type_name(c) != "PrismNode"
            return err("prism_st_dashboard: card " + str(idx) + " is not a PrismNode (got " + type_name(c) + ")")
    prism_arrange.prism_flow(cards)
